<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip Carteret</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1639">1639</a>–<a href="/years/1682">1682</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip Carteret was the first governor of the English Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a> and then of East Jersey, a Jersey-born cousin of the proprietor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-carteret">Sir George Carteret</a>. Arriving in 1665, he governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-new-jersey">Elizabethtown</a>, quarrelled with settlers over quitrents, and clashed with Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-andros">Edmund Andros</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, who had him arrested in 1680. He was soon released and remained governor until 1682.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-carteret.jpg" alt="Philip Carteret" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author 18th century artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philip_Carteret_(1733-1796).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
